From c76fb34021375ecf3d70afb289acad7988577f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <2.03348624e+08+yaegerbomb42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vm): stop EPIPE on exec stdin from killing the server
 (VM-02)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A docker exec whose stdin pipe is closed early (destination is a directory,
workspace full, container gone) emitted EPIPE on the socket with no 'error'
listener, and with no process-level handler the whole Next.js server died —
a remote DoS for any signed-in user via the upload route.

- docker-driver: attach error listeners to every child stdin/stdout/stderr;
  feed exec payloads through stream.pipeline from a chunked Readable so
  large writes honour backpressure, and reject with a typed VmStdinError
  (code EPIPE) instead of leaking an unhandled 'error' event. Reap the CLI
  on failure so a wedged docker process cannot outlive the request.
- lib/runtime/process-guard: last-resort uncaughtException and
  unhandledRejection listeners. Known stream errors are logged and the
  server keeps serving; anything else keeps Node's fatal behaviour.
  Registered once from instrumentation.
- upload route: refuse a destination that already exists as a directory or
  special file with 409 destination_not_a_file, and map an EPIPE-class
  write failure to 409 destination_rejected instead of a 500.
